/*
  Cache policy for the static site.

  The HTML must never be cached hard, or a version bump ships to nobody:
  browsers and CDNs hold on to index.html for a long time by default, and the
  whole point of sync_site.py is that this page describes a build. Everything
  else is content-addressed by nothing, so it gets revalidated.

  Fingerprinted assets would allow immutable caching, but the site is three
  files that change rarely and the fingerprinting would need a build step --
  the thing this site deliberately does not have.
*/

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()

  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, must-revalidate

/version.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
